# Project: Sammon mapping revisited - adaptive weighting, a scalable solver
#          and a temporal extension (alpha-Sammon)
# Authors: Martin Radvansky <martin.radvansky@vsb.cz>
#          Martin Radvansky, Jr. <martin.radvansky1@vsb.cz>
# Affiliation: Department of Computer Science, Faculty of Electrical Engineering
#              and Computer Science, VSB - Technical University of Ostrava
#
# REPOSITORY POLICY: only SOURCE CODE and documentation are versioned.
# The repository deliberately excludes:
#   - all public data (downloaded by the scripts, see README section 4),
#   - all data the project generates itself (synthetic datasets, caches),
#   - all results (CSV files, embeddings, tables, figures, logs) - every one of
#     them is produced by running the code; the archive of the results behind
#     the published paper lives on Zenodo.
# Rule of thumb: if running the code can produce it, it does not belong in git.

# --- virtual environment and bytecode ---
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- input data: downloaded as well as generated ---
# Public datasets are fetched by the scripts (OpenML, UCI, SNAP, SocioPatterns);
# synthetic datasets are generated from the configuration. Both are reproducible.
src/data/
# Exception: the manifest records WHAT is to be downloaded or generated, so it
# is source, not data.
!src/data/manifest.json

# --- results (all reproducible by running the experiments) ---
results/

# --- LaTeX: intermediate files and output PDFs ---
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.spl
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot

# --- working and temporary files ---
*.bak
*.bak_*
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- internal material: not for the public repository ---
# These directories hold working and strategic notes (assessments of acceptance
# chances, journal selection, validation findings, briefs for agents), the
# manuscript itself and third-party PDFs.
documentation/
podklady/
podklady_clanek/
casopisy/
reserse/
projectstate.md
CLAUDE.md
# The manuscript: the publisher receives an exclusive licence and the repository
# is cited for the CODE. Figures and generated numbers are outputs anyway.
# Same policy for the English translation (clanek_en/) - it is not published
# as text either, only cited; and for the internal Czech pre-submission
# review rounds (review_cz_*/), which are working notes, not deliverables.
clanek/
clanek_en/
review_cz_*/
# The authors' 2013 conference papers - copyright IEEE, must not be
# redistributed. README cites them with their DOIs instead.
konference/
# Working pipeline outside src/
pipeline/
# Flat journal-submission packages built by src/tools/make_submission.py -
# regenerated from clanek_en/ + results/tables/ + clanek/, never hand-edited.
submission/

# Editorial Manager (DAMI) submission preparation: cover letter and
# form-field texts. 00_/03_ are hand-written and kept out of git only
# because this is per-submission working material, not a deliverable; 01_/02_
# are regenerated on request by src/tools/make_submission_guide.py once the
# manuscript is final and the Zenodo DOI exists (author instruction,
# 2026-09-18: do not generate them - or commit them - before then).
dami_submission/
